# The keeper image's build context is the repository root (docker/keeper/Dockerfile).
#
# An allow-list, not a deny-list: everything is left out, and only what the
# keeper and its report run on is let back in. A deny-list fails open — a new
# secret file nobody thought to list would go into the context, and from there
# into a layer anyone with the image can read. This way `.env.local` (which
# holds the fork's archive RPC URL), docker/keeper/.env, docker/keeper/secrets/
# and every key or report on the machine can never enter the build.
*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!packages/core/package.json
!packages/core/src
!packages/chain/package.json
!packages/chain/src
!packages/vault/package.json
!packages/vault/src
!packages/vault/scripts
!scripts/env.mjs

# Left out again inside what was let back in: tests, installed dependencies,
# and any environment file, wherever it is.
**/*.test.ts
**/node_modules
**/.env*
